---
code: K0017
title: For Without Arrow
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, loop, for, arrow]
description: "'for' loop header is missing '=>' before its body expression"
---

A `for` loop expression requires `=>` separating the loop header (and optional `fold` accumulator) from the loop body expression.

## Example

This error occurs when a block or expression immediately follows `for ... in ...` without `=>`:

```kura
fn render-list(items: Seq<String>) => {
  for _, item in items {
    #text(item)
  }
}
```

## Solution

Insert `=>` between the `for` header (or `fold` clause) and the body expression:

```kura
fn render-list(items: Seq<String>) => {
  for _, item in items => #text(item)
}

fn sum(xs: Seq<Int>): Int =>
  for _, x in xs fold acc = 0 => acc + x
```

Note that list comprehensions (`[ expr for x in xs ]`) use `[ ... ]` brackets and do not take `=>` or `fold`.
